hello and welcome to the new order of  your source for everything anime and  manga and we are back today to talk  about clovers preferably black ones as  we review the royal knights arc which i  suppose is the black clover take on the  standard shonen tournament arc which was  quite enjoyable i'm always a sucker for  that kind of format yes i am and there  was plenty to like about it but of  course some minor stuff that made me go  a bit  hmm but before we do the thing with the  talking if you're enjoying these black  clover dives and i would highly  encourage you to like this video and  subscribe to the channel numbers are  telling me that you guys seem to be  quite enjoying these videos so do keep  it up because i refuse to read comments  because i know that someone  somewhere is going to spoil something i  know you're out there  let's get into it though the royal  nightstark is probably the most  simplistic story that we've encountered  thus far in black clover and it takes  place almost exclusively in one location  with one core mission statement that we  don't really diverge from that doesn't  say it's a bad thing i'm just very used  to the sudden twists of black clover now  however tournaments are a great shonen  staple almost every battle manga will  feature one in some form of the course  of its publication and it's because  they're kind of a super format  the standard belief is that tournament  arcs get used as an excuse to amp up  action as well as artificially inflate  drama under this kind of construct and  yes that can be true however what's  always struck me as great about  tournament arcs is how they can be used  to showcase character development and  interactions so for example in the royal  nightstark we get to see a whole ton of  bizarre action-based interactions such  as asta vs magna which you would just  never have the opportunity to see  anywhere else because coming up with a  reason for them to fight would be rather  convoluted and tabata does spice things  up quite nicely by mixing up our magic  knight squad so it's not like our  standard black bulls versus golden dawn  which it very easily could have been  instead we get this nice pick and mix a  bit of noel here a bit of you know there  cap it off for the mushroom and mmm  delicious but it results in some really  captivating teams and a lot of fun  dynamics my favorite of which is asta's  team which we will get into  but firstly i do have to say that as  much as i do love tournament arcs i was  kind of disappointed by the setup for  this one mostly because to be perfectly  frank i still don't understand what  we're doing  why we're doing it and even how we're  doing it like i do get that the general  point is to form some sort of super  squad to attack the eye of the midnight  sun which  is cool but why are we doing it with  these specific people we have a total of  48 candidates which are a mixture of  ranks but dominated by rookies with a  couple of vice captains and even one  captain  so how did we make the decision to you  know  get here was this an invitation only  tournament or was it open to anyone who  wanted to be here if so why aren't there  tons of other magic knights vying for  this  allegedly prestigious position  especially the more noble ones which is  like  all of them or why is it this specific  group of the black bulls and not  everyone else you know where's vanessa  go shami charmy well  charmy is here but not to participate  but do you know what i mean and i guess  i could accept the reasoning that the  only people here are the ones with  something to prove but at the same time  that's kind of at odds with the purpose  of the selection exam itself which is to  find the best of the best of the magic  knights in order to pit them against the  greatest threat  currently facing the clover kingdom so  on the one hand we have this profoundly  important purpose and outcome but the  process to get there is almost entirely  frivolous because we have this  completely arbitrary group of people  mostly populated by hothead rookies  competing for this  monumentally important task oh and i  should mention that mr wizard king  states that part of the reason for the  exam was to weed out the unconscious  betrayal which does present itself  within language  language but even then unless you're  going to put the entirety of the magic  knight forces in this situation you're  basically just crossing your fingers and  hoping that the betrayer is one of these  arbitrary people it's just a less than  solid setup but you know what  it's it's also kind of fine i can get  over the structure and the motivations  and everything else because tabitha's  true skill shines in characters and  there is a lot to work with here  starting with someone who almost  automatically became a favorite of mine  being zora i love his design i love his  magic his backstory is appropriately  tragic and everything about him comes  together to form this very compelling  presence and it was very interesting  because at first i thought he was going  to be this perfect philosophical counter  to astor you know our protagonist who  loves teamwork and then hears zoro who  insists on working alone but in the end  the two of them turned out to have an  extraordinarily similar value system  especially when it comes to their ideals  of the magic knights or i suppose in  zora's case his father's ideal of what  the magic knights were which is kind of  mirrored by astor's words in their final  round  i also love the idea that despite his  very villainous design and dickish  nature  zora didn't actually turn out to be our  main antagonist of the aqua really an  antagonist at all he was a fun red  herring in that regard and he turned  into a solid ally quite quickly with he  and astor even giving each other cute  little compliments during their second  match and in the end they were actually  a pretty great team and i would love to  see zora just flat out join the black  balls he's perfect for them being a  lowly peasant outcast who goes against  the grain but that's really the only way  i could see him actually joining the  magic knights because i don't think  there's any other squad that really  embodies his father's ideals with that  said i do also think it was  just a little bit weird that nobody  recognized the fact that zora was  impersonating another magic knight a  vice captain no less  i mean the wizard king sure he's a  cheeky mofo and he'd let something like  this just happen but did nobody else  know what the vice captain of the purple  orcas looked like it was quite shocking  just how easily zora managed to get away  with his facade moving on though also on  team aster we had  mimosa a selection that made me audibly  say quite strongly at first because i  thought that she was just going to be  some sort  of noel replacement who would go on to  spend most of her time doting over astor  and maybe do something useful  on one occasion but that i am happy to  say was not at all the case mimosa was  actually  kind of a boss in this arc she even took  the role of leader in the first round  and had some choice words for her  brother when she stated make sure you  win this match because in the next round  astor and i  intend to slaughter you which is the  kind of determined sass that i really  love  plus she also fit in perfectly with the  whole team dynamic on so many different  levels as well she was great for  protecting the crystal she counted  soul's golem and mimosa was even able to  heal astor which is pretty perfect  because his crowning feature tends to be  how heavily injured he becomes in combat  and it made me realize that in many many  ways mimosa is a much more natural  combat partner for astor than noel and i  guess i just want to say  congratulations to tarbeta for taking a  character that i really did not care for  and turning her into mimosa vermillion  speaking of vermilions or familiai  whatever the collective noun is mimosa's  brother kirsch was a surprising favorite  of mine i mean everything about him is  horrible but in the most hilarious of  ways he's not like noel's siblings that  are just kind of sickening kirsch has a  lot of redemptive qualities just when it  comes to pure comedy and a great  selection of one line is for everyday  use  such as my favorite which is silence  filth you're polluting my  heir but in addition to this he's  actually quite helpful as well giving  magna and soul some very well conveyed  advice regarding how to more effectively  use their magic which was a bit of a  surprise for that kind of character and  of course he does have a change of heart  at the end where he discovers that his  definition of beauty is narrow and  lacking meaning that he should be a  nicer character for us to follow in the  future  maybe probably that's how most of them  tend to go but as for the centerpiece of  the arc this was unexpected but it all  spawns from finral  and langris langris and honestly this  was probably the matchup i was least  excited for because by that point in the  tournament the format was dragging just  a little bit but tabitha clearly felt  that as well and decided to switch  things up by having finra lose and  language go  ever so slightly insane causing a very  high stakes conflict against aston and  his team to commence and so it actually  became the only match in this arc that i  was solidly invested in because it had  the weight of finral behind it and in  retrospect it was also a really great  payoff for the layering that tabitar had  been conducting in previous arcs you  know gradually building finral up  through stuff like the underwater temple  then introducing language at the star  festival and now having all of that work  coming to a boiling point here in this  arc which also gave us a very nice  victory for asta in his  newly controllable transform state  because despite the fact that this match  was officially a tie it wasn't really  about winning in the end more about  making sure that langris was defeated  with his oddly  eye of the midnight sun vibes with that  said the greatest moment of the arc by  far belongs to finral when he sent sekke  directly to army sitting on the toilet  through spatial magic that cooked quite  a lot for me i'm still laughing about it  now  but we also had a captain participating  real of the aqua deers also known as the  suckiest squad now after the black bulls  have broken their losing streak and i do  like his concept quite a bit with the  whole misunderstood artist vibes he's  also pretty terrifying given that his  artistic muse is essentially his  opponent and the stronger his opponent  is the greater the desire to create he's  the sort of character i like because he  does possess amazing power but quite  strict limitations on how it can be used  so he's not  in any way overpowered because he does  have to meet that mental criteria i find  that sort of stuff much more satisfying  than someone with phenomenal power who  can access it easily and use it to  perfection that sort of thing kind of  bores me  which you know is sort of what you know  is becoming after asda's tied the final  matchup sees yuno directly take on a  captain and not only that but he does  win fire a technicality it was real's  fault i guess but i was hoping to see  yuna lose here for the first time i  really wanted him to have his astor  moment of hitting a ceiling then being  forced to go away and figuring out how  to penetrate said sealing but instead  yuno is perfect as per usual which i  suppose  is fine because it does counter  balanceaster's wild imperfection  you know gets to where he is through  seemingly no effort at all meanwhile  aston needs to struggle with all of his  might at every step still makes me think  that yuna must have been born a noble  child though because this natural talent  is very comparable to theirs if not  greater  in fact i would say definitely greater  as for noble children i would be remiss  not to mention that noel got to take a  step forward here by soundly defeating  her brother solid silver which is such  a cool name for such a disappointing  existence and my favorite part of this  whole conflict was seeing the split  panel of noel in the present versus noel  and past because it was a great  indicator of showing how much she's  changed and how ready noah was to take  on solid and she did it so you know what  screw you  solid silver and you are the siblings  you better watch your backs as well and  there were moments of other interests  like klaus's brief moment of growth and  the um  the fungus magic user whose name i don't  remember but it was pretty funny overall  though this arc was pretty  straightforward there were a couple of  surprises as well as a banquet of what  is now becoming the signature topper to  micro flashback and just a lot of  character growth all around which is the  reason why i can look past the more  structural issues of the arc and  in fact the series in general if these  characters were even mildly less well  written then i think i would have lost  interest in black clover a bit of a  while ago however i can't help but want  to read about them i want to see each  and every one of them overcome their  various obstacles in life and tabata has  a great method of allowing a scale of  empathy that you normally  wouldn't find with secondary or even  tertiary characters in very badly  written series you can't even find it  with the primary characters so i'm  guessing we'll find out what the actual  results of this  exam thing were and where this bizarre  trip of individuals is going to be taken  during the next dock so yeah i'ma do  that right now but that pretty much does  it for this blind review of the royal  night sock and what do you guys think  please do leave your thoughts in the  comments below or even join my discord  server and if you're keen for some more  black clover content then please to go  and check out some of my other videos or  even subscribe to the channel for  very maybe regular black clover goodness  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review and i'll see you next time

